WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.530
- [Narrator] A tech industry battle

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.600
is taking shape over the metaverse.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.410
- What is the metaverse?

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.350
- Metaverse.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.780
- In the metaverse.
- Metaverse.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.870
- The metaverse will be the successor

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.000
to the mobile internet.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.370
- [Narrator] A metaverse is essentially

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.910
a massive virtual world

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.720
that can be accessed in real time

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.150
by millions of people using avatars.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.600
The concept is rooted in
science fiction movies

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.620
like "Ready Player One."

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.300
- [Announcer] A whole virtual universe.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.240
- [Narrator] But now it's
playing out in the real world.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.410
Facebook just changed its name to Meta

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.107
to better reflect its
expansion into the metaverse,

00:00:33.107 --> 00:00:35.220
and it joins companies like Roblox,

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.880
Epic Games and Microsoft,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.390
and planning to spend billions

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.890
to be at the forefront of
building out these virtual realms.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.740
- I think we're still in the
beginning stages of this.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.400
And so a lot of what's happening

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.610
is still just competition, if you will,

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:49.650
between the companies

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.030
to establish themselves in the metaverse.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.210
- [Narrator] But how exactly
will the metaverse work?

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.130
And why do tech giants see
it as the next evolution

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:58.993
of the internet?

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.380
- For the metaverse, it is a convergence

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.930
of physical and digital,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.590
almost like your digital
lifestyle catching up

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.870
to your physical lifestyle in some ways.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.650
- [Narrator] Cathy Hackl is
the chief metaverse officer

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.510
and CEO of the Future Intelligence Group,

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.170
a consulting company that
provides strategic insight

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.050
for companies navigating
the metaverse space.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.900
- It is enabled by many
different technologies,

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.160
like augmented reality, virtual reality,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.500
blockchain, obviously NFTs
play a big part there.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.900
AI, 5G, cloud computing.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.850
So it's not just about technology,

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.340
it's not just one thing.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.910
- [Narrator] For now, most
metaverse virtual spaces

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.020
will look more like the inside

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.980
of a video game than real life.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.810
And some big tech executives
envision the metaverse

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.320
as an interoperable open platform.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.830
This means no one company

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.560
or organization will own it,

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.770
and avatars will be able to move freely

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.370
between metaverse virtual spaces.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.420
- There's all these different platforms

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.630
and the question is sort

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.300
of how do you connect all those?

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.760
And whether it's gonna be possible

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.140
to jump from you have
your avatar in Roblox,

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.620
can you somehow cross through

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.190
and get to Facebook through that?

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.010
Are the platforms gonna be connected?

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:10.960
- [Narrator] In some ways,

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.850
the metaverse is already here.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:14.600
Immersive games like Fortnite

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.390
and gaming platforms like Roblox

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.560
include metaverse-like elements

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.300
where gamers can use avatars

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.110
to play games and attend events

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.040
or use digital currency to buy products.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.280
- Roblox and Fortnite,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.670
so they kind of, I guess some would say

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.840
have like authority

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.100
because they already have
these huge user bases

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.870
and they have the platform developed.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.910
They're not building
something from scratch.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.370
And so I think that's a
huge advantage for them.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.060
So they're really just I think focused

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.300
on developing these in-app experiences

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.680
or these games.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.180
- [Narrator] For instance,
Roblox recently unveiled

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.160
what will be a huge overhaul
for its avatar system,

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.630
allowing players to be more
life like and customizable.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.665
- Our vision goes well beyond play.

00:02:55.665 --> 00:02:59.371
We're imagining a place
where people learn together,

00:02:59.371 --> 00:03:01.660
where people work together.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.260
- [Narrator] Meanwhile, Epic Games,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.404
which owns Fortnite,

00:03:04.404 --> 00:03:07.130
announced it raised $1 billion in funding

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.720
to support its vision for the metaverse.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.070
- They recently made announcements

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.480
that they're gonna start to
look at potentially working

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.300
with blockchain developers,

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.640
so that in itself is a big signal

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.250
of some level of openness.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.870
- [Narrator] Facebook's name
change reflects its ambition

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.580
of being a big player
in the metaverse race.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.160
- We believe the metaverse

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.970
will be the successor
to the mobile internet.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.890
We'll be able to feel present,

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.340
like we're right there with people,

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.740
no matter how far apart we actually are.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.390
- [Narrator] The company,
which already owns Oculus VR,

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:41.190
is spending billions on
other VR company acquisitions

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.610
and hardware development.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.430
And it plans to create 10,000 jobs

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.890
in the European Union
over the next five years

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.730
to build the virtual space.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.340
- We expect to invest
many billions of dollars

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.410
for years to come before
the metaverse reaches scale.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.460
- [Narrator] The company's expansion

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.380
into the metaverse comes
amid intense criticism

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.520
over revelations

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.750
in The Wall Street Journal
Facebook File series,

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.130
which showed the company
knows its platforms

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.340
are riddled with flaws that cause harm.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.600
CEO Mark Zuckerberg has said the criticism

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.360
paints a false picture of
the company he co-founded.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.651
- It would be in the best
interests of the company

00:04:14.651 --> 00:04:16.110
to kind of make sure

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.770
that they maybe distance themselves

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:19.620
from the Facebook app,

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.950
and some of the things
that have come to light.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.070
- [Narrator] Zuckerberg says
the name change reflects

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.210
the company's goals

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.700
to move beyond social media apps.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.150
- Building our social media apps

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.420
will always be an important focus for us.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.520
But right now, our brand
is so tightly linked

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.680
to one product

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.820
that it can't possibly
represent everything

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.130
that we're doing today,
let alone in the future.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.596
- [Narrator] Other
companies like Microsoft

00:04:43.596 --> 00:04:46.665
are focusing on strategic
game company acquisitions

00:04:46.665 --> 00:04:48.370
that could give them a foothold

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:49.740
in the metaverse space.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.620
The company already have a
history in the gaming world.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.990
It created the popular
video game console Xbox.

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:00.290
- They closed like a $7.5 billion deal

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.690
on the video game company
ZeniMax Media earlier this year.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.060
And they also were previously in talks

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.080
to buy Discord.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.170
- [Narrator] And in March,

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:14.030
Microsoft announced its new
Microsoft Mesh platform,

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.750
which enables shared
experiences on any device

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.120
through mixed reality applications.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.200
Accelerated interest in the metaverse

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.240
was fueled in part by the pandemic.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.260
While stuck inside, people
spent more time online.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.330
Roblox reported 42.1
million daily active users

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.193
in Q1 of 2021,

00:05:32.193 --> 00:05:36.420
a 78% increase from the
same time the previous year.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.730
- So the pandemic really kind

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.060
of set us forward a couple years

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.930
in people understanding the convergence

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:43.564
of digital and physical.

00:05:43.564 --> 00:05:45.430
And really for us to really think

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.450
about the future of the internet.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.760
What comes next?

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.230
- [Narrator] For now, the shared ambitions

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.780
of these giant corporations

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.280
are setting the stage
for a high-stakes race

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.360
to create this digital world.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.150
- The metaverse is gonna
impact every vertical

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.790
and every industry in some way.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.330
That's gonna impact the way we socialize,

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:03.230
the way we work, the way we have fun.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:06.619
So it is gonna touch almost
every aspect of our lives.

00:06:06.619 --> 00:06:09.286
(pensive music)

